{"step_index":1454,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:20:45Z","input_tokens":2413,"cache_read_tokens":205743,"output_tokens":1163,"content":"Support for both **standard `AIzaSy` API keys** and **`AQ.` OAuth / Bearer tokens** has been implemented across the backend and frontend.\n\n---\n\n### Implementation Details\n\n1. **Backend REST Caller ([`server.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py#L90-L165))**:\n   - Added `call_gemini_rest` using `httpx` to dynamically format headers and URLs based on key prefix:\n     ```python\n     if api_key.startswith(\"AQ.\"):\n         # Treat as Google Cloud OAuth / Bearer Token\n         headers = {\n             \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {api_key}\",\n             \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n         }\n         url = f\"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model_name}:generateContent\"\n     else:\n         # Standard AIzaSy key passed via header\n         headers = {\n             \"x-goog-api-key\": api_key,\n             \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n         }\n         url = f\"https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/{model_name}:generateContent\"\n     ```\n   - Automatically accepts tokens passed via either the `x-api-key` header or the standard `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header in [`/api/analyze-bill`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/server.py#L167-L200).\n\n2. **Backend Tax Advisor ([`utils/tax_suggestions.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/tax_suggestions.py#L92-L115))**:\n   - Updated the Gemini caller to dispatch `Authorization: Bearer` for `AQ.` tokens and `x-goog-api-key` for `AIzaSy` keys.\n\n3. **Client-Side Multimodal Extraction ([`utils/aiExtractor.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js#L72-L78))**:\n   - Passes `Authorization: Bearer <key>` when sending `AQ.` tokens to `/api/analyze-bill`.\n   - In direct client-side fallback calls ([`aiExtractor.js#L136-L150`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js#L136-L150)), formats headers as `Authorization: Bearer ${key}` for `AQ.` tokens and `x-goog-api-key` for `AIzaSy` keys without returning 401.\n\n4. **Client-Side Tax Suggestions ([`utils/taxSuggestions.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/taxSuggestions.js#L54-L72)) & UI Modal ([`components/ApiKeyModal.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/ApiKeyModal.js#L21-L30))**:\n   - Updated client-side AI suggestions and input fields to support both key formats.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n\nAll authentication test suites passed:\n- **`AQ.` Bearer Token:** Dispatches `Authorization: Bearer AQ...` $\\rightarrow$ 200 OK.\n- **`AIzaSy` API Key:** Dispatches `x-goog-api-key: AIzaSy...` $\\rightarrow$ 200 OK.\n- Both `Authorization: Bearer` and `x-api-key` request headers verified with FastAPI `TestClient`.\n\nThe FastAPI server is live at:\n- **Application URL:** [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000)","thinking":"All modified files were inspected for clickable `file://` links and adherence to specified guidelines. The goal is ensuring proper formatting and functionality across all codebase components. Verification continues on remaining files.\n\n\n"}
{"step_index":1455,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:30:39Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nCRITICAL PARSER REFACTOR: IMPLEMENT 3-TIER PRODUCTION INVOICE EXTRACTION PIPELINE\n\nRefactor our invoice parsing pipeline across backend and client fallback to eliminate brittle line-by-line regex. Implement these 3 steps:\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 1: TABLE-ANCHOR BOUNDARY SLICING (in invoiceTextParser.js / parser logic)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStop running OCR regex top-to-bottom across the entire document text. Instead, slice the document into 3 distinct vertical zones:\n1. HEADER ZONE (Top to Table Start):\n   - Start: Beginning of text.\n   - End: Table Header row containing at least two keywords: ['Description', 'Item', 'Particulars', 'HSN', 'Qty', 'Rate', 'Amount'].\n   - Purpose: Extract Vendor Name, GSTIN, Invoice Number, and Date ONLY.\n   - Guardrail: Never extract any line from this zone as an item, even if it contains numbers, addresses ('Shop No', 'Plot', 'Bazaar'), or phone numbers.\n\n2. LINE ITEM ZONE (Strict Table Boundaries):\n   - Start: Immediately after the Table Header row.\n   - End: Table Footer row matching: ['Subtotal', 'Item Subtotal', 'Taxable Value', 'Total Tax', 'CGST', 'SGST', 'IGST', 'Total in Words'].\n   - Purpose: Extract ONLY physical products/services strictly located between these two boundaries. Discard any line without a valid product name and positive rate/amount.\n\n3. SUMMARY & TAX ZONE (Table End to Bottom):\n   - Start: Subtotal / Tax rows down to the end of the text.\n   - Purpose: Extract Subtotal, CGST, SGST, IGST, and the printed Grand Total ('Invoice Total Demanded', 'Net Payable', 'Grand Total').\n   - Guardrail: Bank details, payment notes, and terms & conditions belong here and must never leak into items.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 2: RIGHT-TO-LEFT (REVERSE) NUMERIC COLUMN PARSER (for Line Item extraction)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDo not parse table lines from left to right, because descriptions often contain numbers (e.g., '20W', '2.5 sq mm', '90m') that fool column splitters.\n\nFor every line within the LINE ITEM ZONE, parse tokens from RIGHT TO LEFT:\n1. Clean commas from numbers (treat commas strictly as thousands separators, e.g., '2,535.00' -> 2535.0, '1,270.00' -> 1270.0).\n2. Scan for numbers starting from the end of the line:\n   - Token 1 (Last Number) = Billed Amount (total_amount)\n   - Token 2 (Second-to-Last Number) = Unit Rate (unit_rate)\n   - Token 3 (Third-to-Last Number) = Quantity (quantity)\n   - Token 4 (Optional Number) = HSN/SAC code (4 to 8 digits)\n3. Everything remaining to the left of these numeric tokens = Description.\n4. Validation Check:\n   - Discard the line if (quantity * unit_rate) deviates by more than 5% from total_amount unless a known discount column exists.\n   - Strip leading/trailing punctuation and unit abbreviations ('NOS', 'PCS', '|', '[', ']').\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSTEP 3: GEMINI VISION MULTIMODAL EXTRACTION AS PRIMARY (FastAPI / Backend)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEnsure client-side text parsing is strictly a fallback. Route the primary extraction through Gemini 2.5 Flash using direct visual layout understanding:\n\n1. Send the file bytes directly (image/jpeg, image/png, or application/pdf) using the Gemini 2.5 Flash model with temperature=0.0.\n2. Support both API key formats in headers:\n   - If key starts with 'AQ.': pass as Authorization: Bearer <key>\n   - Otherwise: pass as x-goog-api-key: <key>\n3. Use a structured JSON schema:\n   {\n     \"vendor_name\": string,\n     \"gstin\": string,\n     \"invoice_number\": string,\n     \"items\": [\n       {\"description\": string, \"quantity\": number, \"unit_rate\": number, \"total_amount\": number}\n     ],\n     \"subtotal\": number,\n     \"cgst\": number,\n     \"sgst\": number,\n     \"igst\": number,\n     \"declared_total\": number\n   }\n4. Post-processing reconciliation:\n   - Ensure declared_total matches the printed total on the bill. If declared_total is suspiciously less than 50% of subtotal (e.g., extracting an HSN/tax fragment like 774 or 20), recalculate declared_total = subtotal + cgst + sgst + igst.\n   - Synchronize property names: set both `declared_total` and `total_declared` to the same value so the frontend audit engine never receives undefined.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-03T01:00:39+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":1456,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:30:40Z","input_tokens":2356,"cache_read_tokens":208197,"output_tokens":1252,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe document structure seems to require a vertical slicing strategy, dividing it into header, line item, and summary/tax zones. This approach aims to isolate specific data types within defined boundaries. The header zone focuses on vendor and invoice metadata, while the line item zone is confined to the table's structure for product/service details. The summary zone handles subtotals, tax details, and the grand total. This method is designed to prevent data leakage between sections.\n\n\nThe initial left-to-right parsing approach for table lines is problematic due to number-containing descriptions. Parsing should proceed right-to-left. This reversed direction will start by identifying the billed amount, unit rate, and quantity numbers. Then, any remaining text is treated as a description. Validating the calculation will ensure data integrity; otherwise, it will be discarded unless it's a known discount column.\n\nGemini Vision will be the primary extraction method, utilizing direct visual layout understanding.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":150,"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js","StartLine":1}}]}
{"step_index":1457,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:30:54Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-03T01:00:54+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-03T01:00:54+05:30\nShowing lines 1-150 of 418\n1: // Client-Side Invoice Text Parser\n2: // Takes raw OCR or PDF text and extracts real structured fields without hallucinating fake items\n3: \n4: import { round2 } from \"./auditEngine.js\";\n5: import { cleanExtractedItems } from \"./itemCleaner.js\";\n6: \n7: /**\n8:  * Standard Indian GSTIN Regex\n9:  */\n10: const GSTIN_REGEX = /\\b[0-9]{2}[A-Z]{5}[0-9]{4}[A-Z]{1}[1-9A-Z]{1}Z[0-9A-Z]{1}\\b/i;\n11: \n12: /**\n13:  * Common Date patterns (DD/MM/YYYY, DD-MM-YYYY, DD.MM.YYYY, DD Month YYYY)\n14:  */\n15: const DATE_REGEX = /\\b(\\d{1,2})[-/\\.](\\d{1,2})[-/\\.](\\d{2,4})\\b|\\b(\\d{1,2})\\s+(Jan|Feb|Mar|Apr|May|Jun|Jul|Aug|Sep|Oct|Nov|Dec)[a-z]*[\\s,]+(\\d{2,4})\\b/i;\n16: \n17: /**\n18:  * Clean currency string to a float number:\n19:  * Strip currency symbols and whitespace, then strip commas BEFORE converting to number\n20:  */\n21: export function parseIndianCurrency(val) {\n22:   if (!val) return 0;\n23:   // Strip currency symbols and whitespace, then strip commas BEFORE converting to number\n24:   const cleaned = String(val).replace(/[₹\\s]/g, '').replace(/,/g, '');\n25:   const num = parseFloat(cleaned);\n26:   return isNaN(num) ? 0 : num;\n27: }\n28: \n29: /**\n30:  * Words-to-number parser for Indian invoices (e.g. 'FOUR THOUSAND FOUR HUNDRED AND NINETY' -> 4490.0)\n31:  */\n32: export function parseWordsToNumber(text) {\n33:   if (!text) return 0;\n34:   const upper = String(text).toUpperCase().replace(/[^A-Z\\s]/g, ' ');\n35:   const words = upper.split(/\\s+/);\n36: \n37:   const units = {\n38:     ZERO: 0, ONE: 1, TWO: 2, THREE: 3, FOUR: 4,\n39:     FIVE: 5, SIX: 6, SEVEN: 7, EIGHT: 8, NINE: 9,\n40:     TEN: 10, ELEVEN: 11, TWELVE: 12, THIRTEEN: 13,\n41:     FOURTEEN: 14, FIFTEEN: 15, SIXTEEN: 16, SEVENTEEN: 17,\n42:     EIGHTEEN: 18, NINETEEN: 19\n43:   };\n44:   const tens = {\n45:     TWENTY: 20, THIRTY: 30, FORTY: 40, FIFTY: 50,\n46:     SIXTY: 60, SEVENTY: 70, EIGHTY: 80, NINETY: 90\n47:   };\n48:   const multipliers = {\n49:     HUNDRED: 100,\n50:     THOUSAND: 1000,\n51:     LAKH: 100000,\n52:     LAKHS: 100000,\n53:     CRORE: 10000000,\n54:     CRORES: 10000000\n55:   };\n56: \n57:   let total = 0;\n58:   let current = 0;\n59:   let found = false;\n60: \n61:   for (const w of words) {\n62:     if (units[w] !== undefined) {\n63:       current += units[w];\n64:       found = true;\n65:     } else if (tens[w] !== undefined) {\n66:       current += tens[w];\n67:       found = true;\n68:     } else if (w === 'HUNDRED') {\n69:       if (current === 0) current = 1;\n70:       current *= 100;\n71:       found = true;\n72:     } else if (multipliers[w] !== undefined) {\n73:       const mult = multipliers[w];\n74:       if (current === 0) current = 1;\n75:       total += current * mult;\n76:       current = 0;\n77:       found = true;\n78:     }\n79:   }\n80: \n81:   total += current;\n82:   return found ? total : 0;\n83: }\n84: \n85: /**\n86:  * Checks if raw text contains commercial invoice keywords\n87:  */\n88: export function isLikelyInvoice(text) {\n89:   if (!text || text.trim().length < 15) return false;\n90: \n91:   const invoiceKeywords = [\n92:     \"invoice\", \"tax invoice\", \"bill\", \"cash memo\", \"parcha\", \"challan\",\n93:     \"gst\", \"gstin\", \"subtotal\", \"total\", \"grand total\", \"qty\", \"rate\", \n94:     \"amount\", \"hsn\", \"cgst\", \"sgst\", \"igst\", \"balance\", \"payable\", \"rupees\", \"mrp\"\n95:   ];\n96: \n97:   const lower = text.toLowerCase();\n98:   let matches = 0;\n99:   for (const kw of invoiceKeywords) {\n100:     if (lower.includes(kw)) matches++;\n101:   }\n102: \n103:   // At least 2 invoice keywords or a valid GSTIN pattern must be present\n104:   return matches >= 2 || GSTIN_REGEX.test(text);\n105: }\n106: \n107: /**\n108:  * Parses raw text into structured Invoice JSON matching our application schema\n109:  */\n110: export function parseInvoiceText(rawText, sourceFileName = \"Uploaded Bill\") {\n111:   const lines = rawText\n112:     .split(/\\r?\\n/)\n113:     .map(l => l.trim())\n114:     .filter(l => l.length > 0);\n115: \n116:   const unreadable_fields = [];\n117: \n118:   // 2. Extract GSTIN\n119:   const gstinMatch = rawText.match(GSTIN_REGEX);\n120:   const gstin = gstinMatch ? gstinMatch[0].toUpperCase() : null;\n121:   if (!gstin) unreadable_fields.push(\"gstin\");\n122: \n123:   // 3. Extract Invoice Number\n124:   let invoice_no = null;\n125:   for (const line of lines) {\n126:     const invMatch = line.match(/(?:inv(?:oice)?|bill|memo|parcha|challan)[\\s#.:\\-_]+([A-Za-z0-9\\/-]+)/i);\n127:     if (invMatch && invMatch[1] && invMatch[1].length >= 2) {\n128:       invoice_no = invMatch[1].trim();\n129:       break;\n130:     }\n131:   }\n132:   if (!invoice_no) {\n133:     // Look for standalone alphanumeric code\n134:     const fallbackMatch = rawText.match(/\\b([A-Z]{2,4}\\/[\\d]{2,4}\\/[\\d]+)\\b/);\n135:     if (fallbackMatch) invoice_no = fallbackMatch[1];\n136:     else unreadable_fields.push(\"invoice_no\");\n137:   }\n138: \n139:   // 4. Extract Date\n140:   let date = null;\n141:   const dateMatch = rawText.match(DATE_REGEX);\n142:   if (dateMatch) {\n143:     date = dateMatch[0].trim();\n144:   } else {\n145:     unreadable_fields.push(\"date\");\n146:   }\n147: \n148:   // 5. Extract Vendor Name (usually the prominent text in the first 3 lines)\n149:   let vendor_name = null;\n150:   for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(5, lines.length); i++) {"}
